-- title:
--   Node places, crossing models and residue-disc cover at full level
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; $\mathcal M =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` of level $M'$ inside Laurent series, and $\mathcal F =$ `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ cut out by the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbf Z/q^2M')^\times$. The element $\bar j \in \mathcal F$ is the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ under the coefficient embedding $\mathbb Q \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$, viewed in $\mathcal M$ and then transported by the inclusion furnished by `hle`, and $J =$ [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) is the $q$-rescaled $q$-expansion of $j$. For a place $P$ (a valuation subring of a field, proper, containing the base field, with principal ideals), `P.ord` is $-\log$ of its adic valuation, `P.evalAt f` is the residue of $f$ at $P$ pulled back to the base field along the inverse of the structure map, and `P.IsRational` says that structure map is surjective onto the residue field.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q \ge 5$; a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ which, by `hW`, is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places; the inclusion `hle` of $\mathcal M$ in $\mathcal F$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathcal M$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring of $\mathcal M$ inducing $A$ on $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, the scaling clause, and a place map preserving degrees and pushing forward divisors of functions with non-zero residue); the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that a Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image lies in $\mathcal M$ lies in $R_0$-integers and has residue the coefficientwise reduction $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ of that series; and a chosen $s \in W$.
--
--   **The small field and its layers.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ`, stating that every element of $A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Auxiliary data: a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. A family of layers: a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $A_n = A \cap K_n$, an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$, and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$. A tame parameter: $\pi_t \in A$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q$, together with `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with trivial tame character `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Finally the base layer: an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $A_b = A \cap K_b$, and a generator $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The field $\mathcal F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is then universally quantified over an intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq \mathcal F$ and over a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, and has the shape (LEVEL) $\Rightarrow$ (MODEL) $\Rightarrow$ (CONCLUSION).
--
--   **(LEVEL), the level-field hypotheses on $F_0$** (four clauses): $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; the compositum of the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $F_0$ is all of $\mathcal F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and linear disjointness: for every $K'$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   **(MODEL), the descended model data on $W_0$** (a conjunction of six groups, the last two of which are themselves long; all its clauses are summarised here in order). (M1) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$. (M2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (M3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal. (M4) Reduction dictionary at $s$: for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in the $R_0$-integers, if $g$ has non-negative order at every place of $\mathcal M$ at which $\bar j$ has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals `s.evalAt` of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $g$ and of $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (M5) $W_0$ is stable under the level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$, membership of $f$ in $W_0$ is equivalent to membership of its image. (M6) There are a subring $B \subseteq \mathcal F$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that: the structure map agrees with $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F$ on $A_b$; $B$ is contained in the compositum $\bar K_b \cdot F_0$ of the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B$ is contained in $W_0$ (each of its elements lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$); $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, i.e. $f \in W_0$ iff $f h = g$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; $\bar j \in B$; $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; there is an element $b \in B \cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $\bar j$, and at which $\bar j$ is not a root of any monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ modulo the maximal ideal of $V$; for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \neq s$ there is likewise an element $b \in B \cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the analogue of (M4) at $s'$ with $V$ in place of $W_0$; for every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with $\#C_s = 2\,$`placeWidthChar q M' s`, kernel $(\varpi_b)$, reduction-compatibility on $A_b$, surjectivity up to fractions, image exactly the image of the Drinfeld coordinate ring, and equivariance of $\rho$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), intertwining `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` with [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16); and, finally, a node package: $\bar j$ lies in the $R_0$-integers with residue in the valuation subring of $s$, $J \in \mathcal F$, there is $a_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A(a_0)^q =$ `s.evalAt` of the residue of $\bar j$, and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with: $\#\,\mathrm{nodes} = q+1$; a common subring $B_c$, generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every $\mathcal O \in \mathrm{nodes}$, each $\mathcal O$ being the localisation of $B_c$ at those of its elements that are units of $\mathcal O$; permutation of `nodes` by the level automorphisms, and transitivity of that action through $\Gamma_0(M')$; pairwise separation (for $\mathcal O \neq \mathcal O'$ some common element is a non-unit of the one and a unit of the other); a valuative cover, namely every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the analogue of (M4) at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node $\mathcal O$; and, for each node $\mathcal O$: $\mathcal O \subseteq W_0$, $\mathcal O$ is local and Noetherian, induces $A$ on $k_0$, every element of $\mathcal O$ is congruent to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (their difference is a non-unit), and there exist $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}(q,M',s)} v$ for a unit $v$ of $k_0 \cap A$, elements $c_x, c_y \in \mathcal O$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ at $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$, $\iota$ sends constants from $k_0 \cap A$ to constants, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ is a unit there, the Hasse datum $J - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $\mathcal O$ with $\iota(J-a_0) = w_V V^e$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e \ge 1$, there is an Igusa branch $W_x$ (a discrete valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal O$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t$ whose reduction is transcendental in the stated polynomial sense, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal and $c_y$ a unit, satisfying a reduction dictionary relating vanishing of $R_0$-residues to the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and, over $s$, membership in $\mathcal O$ together with non-unit congruences, and separating $\mathcal O$ from every other node), and there is a node chart $B_x \subseteq \mathcal O \cap B$ whose elements have non-negative order wherever $\bar j$ does, with $\mathcal O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, $B_x$ generating $F_0$ by fractions, $B_x$ generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $\bar j$ with the monic-polynomial clause above, and fails to contain $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **(CONCLUSION).** For every field $F_{SS}$ with a $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\mathcal F$ to $F_{SS}$ (a valuation subring of $\mathcal F$ inducing $A$ on $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, with surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is its maximal ideal, plus the scaling clause) such that $R$-integrality cuts out $W_0$ on $F_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with $\#N = q+1$, and there exist: a family of fields $F_{I,x}$ indexed by the places $x$ of $F_{SS}$, each a $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebra, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ from $\mathcal F$ to $F_{I,x}$, places $b_x$ of $F_{I,x}$; subrings $C'_l \subseteq A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ ($l \in \iota$), each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_{c,l}$ with elements $\pi_l$, exponents $E_l$ and an exponent $E_0$; sets $S(nd)$ of places of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, subrings $\mathcal N(nd)$ of $\mathcal F$, and local Noetherian subrings $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ of $\mathcal F$, indexed by the places $nd$ of $F_{SS}$; and functions $c_x, c_y, c_u$ from places of $F_{SS}$ to $\mathcal F$, subject to the following.
--
--   First, $C'_n = A \cap K_n$ (an element of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $C'_n$ iff it lies in $A$ and in the image of $K_n$); for $d \in C'_l$ the residue of $d$ in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ vanishes iff $\varpi'_l \mid d$; $C'_{n_0} \le C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0} \neq 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l \ge 1$; every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with trivial tame character fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; and $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0} = v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ for some $w \ge 1$ and some unit $v$ of $A$.
--
--   Second, for every $nd \in N$: $b_{nd}$ and $nd$ are rational places, as is every $P \in S(nd)$; $\mathcal N(nd)$ consists exactly of those $f$ that lie in the $R_{nd}$-integers, in the $R$-integers, and in every $P \in S(nd)$; for $f \in \mathcal N(nd)$ and $P \in S(nd)$ one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$; $c_x(nd)\,c_y(nd) = (\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0} c_u(nd)$; the $R_{nd}$-residue of $c_x(nd)$ vanishes, $nd.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $c_x(nd)$ equals $1$, the $R$-residue of $c_y(nd)$ vanishes, and $b_{nd}.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R_{nd}$-residue of $c_y(nd)$ equals $1$ (each clause conditional on the relevant integrality); for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the arithmetic Galois semilinear automorphism $g$ attached to $\tau$ on the base-changed function field of level $q^2M'$ and `levelH q M'` preserves $S(nd)$ and fixes $c_x(nd)$ and $c_y(nd)$; every $f \in \mathcal F$ is a quotient of elements of some $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$, and also satisfies $f b = \sum_i c_i a_i$ for some non-zero $b$ and finitely many $a_i$ in $\mathcal N_0(nd,n_0)$ with coefficients $c_i \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$; and for every layer $l$: $\mathcal N_0(nd,n_0) \le \mathcal N_0(nd,l) \le \mathcal N(nd)$; $S(nd)$ is exactly the set of places containing $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ and sending its non-units into the maximal ideal of $A$; $C'_l$ maps into $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$; every element of $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ is congruent to an element of $C'_l$; families of elements of $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ with $C'_l$-linearly independent $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients summing to zero vanish; there is a subring $B_x \subseteq \mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ containing $c_x(nd), c_y(nd), c_u(nd)$, with $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ its localisation at its units and $B_x$ generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x(nd), c_y(nd) \in \mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ and $c_u(nd)$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W_{c,l}$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ and an isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel` $(W_{c,l}, \pi_l^{E_l})$ such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c \circ \sigma$ is the constant embedding, every element of $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and the two order dictionaries hold: an $f \in \mathcal N_0(nd,l)$ whose $R_{nd}$-residue is non-zero of order $n$ at $b_{nd}$ satisfies $\iota_c(f) \equiv \gamma V^n$ modulo $(\pi_l, U)$ for a unit $\gamma$, and one whose $R$-residue is non-zero of order $n$ at $nd$ satisfies $\iota_c(f) \equiv \gamma U^n$ modulo $(\pi_l, V)$.
--
--   Third, the sets $S(nd)$ for $nd \in N$ are pairwise disjoint; for $nd \in N$ and $P \in S(nd)$, every $f$ in the $R_0$-integers with non-negative order wherever $\bar j$ has, whose residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, satisfies $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of its image minus $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ for every $a \in A$ reducing to `s.evalAt` of that residue. For each $\zeta'$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on places of $F_{SS}$ preserving $N$, matching $S$ and the level action and carrying the integers of $R_{nd}$ to those of $R_{\tau_N(nd)}$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves the $R$-integers, the induced residual automorphism carries $N$ into $N$ and $S(nd)$ (as a set of places, via `smulDisc`) to $S$ of the translated place. Every element of the $R_0$-integers maps into the $R_{nd}$-integers; and for each $nd \in N$ there is a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to $F_{I,nd}$ compatible with $R_0$- and $R_{nd}$-residues and such that membership in the valuation subring of $s$ corresponds to membership in that of $b_{nd}$.
--
--   Fourth, the Hasse datum: $J \in \mathcal F$ and there is $a_0 \in A$ with $J - a_0$ in the $R$-integers of residue $0$, with $\mathrm{res}_A(a_0)^q =$ `s.evalAt (jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M')`, and with some $c' \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ such that $c'(J-a_0)$ lies in the $R$-integers with non-zero residue and, for every $nd \in N$, $J - a_0$ lies in the $R_{nd}$-integers with non-zero residue and $nd.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $c'(J-a_0)$ equals minus $b_{nd}.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R_{nd}$-residue of $J-a_0$.
--
--   Fifth, separation of the node places: for $x \in N$ and any place $y \notin N$ of $F_{SS}$ there is $g$ in the $R$-integers and in $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$, a non-unit there, with $R$-residue non-zero of order $0$ at $y$, and integral at every rational place of $\mathcal F$ at which $\bar j$ has non-negative order; and for $x \neq x'$ in $N$ there is $g$ lying in $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$ as $c_x(x)$ times a unit and lying in $\mathcal N_0(x',n_0)$ as a unit.
--
--   Finally, the covering statement: every rational place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying the congruence condition at $s$ (for every $f$ in the $R_0$-integers with non-negative order wherever $\bar j$ has and residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a \in A$ reducing to `s.evalAt` of that residue, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$) either belongs to $S(nd)$ for some $nd \in N$, or lies in a residue disc: there are a place $Q \notin N$ of $F_{SS}$, a set $D$ of places of $\mathcal F$ and $z \in \mathcal F$ with $P \in D$ such that `R.IsResidueDisc Q D z` holds, that is, $z$ is a disc coordinate for $R$ at $Q$ on $D$ (the places of $D$ are rational, $z$ is integral with residue of absolute value $<1$ at each, $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $z$ is $1$, each $c$ of absolute value $<1$ is the value of $z$ at a unique place of $D$, $z$ minus its value has order $1$ at each place of $D$, and non-zero functions of order $0$ throughout $D$ have constant absolute value there), the reduction is pointwise compatible on $D$, and the degree formula of `DegreeOn` holds.
--
--   This is the passage from the descended level-field model of the curve at a supersingular place $s$ — affine chart over $A \cap k_0$, $q+1$ node local rings with $UV = \pi_0^{E_0}$ crossing presentations, Igusa branches and node charts — to the intrinsic package on the base-changed function field at full level $q^2M'$: the $q+1$ node places of the special fibre with their layered crossing models, level- and inertia-equivariance, the Hasse datum on the moduli invariant, and the covering of the remaining rational places by residue discs. It is used by the single-existential $k$-level constructor [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart), which packages the semistable reduction of the modular curve at $q$ needed for the level-lowering step.
